From 3444f52ca8b38cd24a96c6b0369d272ae95d5b9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:44:07 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add client combat animation system driven by
 CombatStateChanged

- CombatAnimationConfig: animation IDs per weapon and common, slot
  priorities/looping, settings; placeholder IDs ("rbxassetid://0") are skipped.
- CombatAnimationController: loads, caches and preloads tracks, plays Attack,
  Block, Stun and Dodge only after the server confirms the state change,
  stops on Idle/Dead/respawn, warns when an attack animation length differs
  from the server swing timing.
- CombatController: stop playing the swing animation on request; the animation
  now starts only after server confirmation.
- CombatConfig: remove per-weapon AnimationId (moved to CombatAnimationConfig).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLMaP4V7LcPHCrxoi4fJm8
